;; =============================================================================
;; Spec: Ariadne step 2d — merge and deploy become granted, transacted effects
;; =============================================================================
;;
;; Normative refs: docs/architecture/rfc-ariadne-adoption.md (adoption
;; step 2 — "grants on the irreversible effects (merge, deploy,
;; spend)"); Ariadne §13.5. Spend is handled by 2b's cost constraint
;; rather than a per-call proposal record — see the description.

{:spec/title "Ariadne step 2d: migrate merge and deploy onto the granted, transacted path"

 :spec/description
 "Move the two discrete irreversible effects — PR merge and cluster
  deploy — onto 2c's transaction coordinator, requiring a 2a grant
  checked by 2b's decide().

  WHY THESE TWO, AND WHY NOT SPEND THE SAME WAY. Merge and deploy are
  DISCRETE effects: one decision, one external mutation, one outcome to
  reconcile — the shape a proposal record fits. Spend is CONTINUOUS:
  minting a proposal record per LLM call would add a disk write to
  every token and reconcile nothing useful. Spend is bounded correctly
  by 2b — a :constraint/max-cost-usd on the grant, checked at decide()
  and re-checked at commit. That is a deliberate split, not an
  oversight.

  MERGE — what changes (source-verified today's state):
    * `pr-lifecycle/merge.clj` `merge-pr!` unconditionally passes
      --auto and returns {:merged? true}. After this spec, enabling
      auto-merge produces an :effect/state of :committing with the
      proposal recorded, NOT a merged claim. The merged event is
      published only after `reconcile!` observes the merge on GitHub.
    * The merge SHA stops coming from local `git rev-parse HEAD` and
      starts coming from the reconciled `gh pr view --json mergeCommit`.
      A SHA the code cannot substantiate is not published.
    * `evaluate-merge-readiness` stays as a pre-flight self-check but
      is no longer the authority — the grant + envelope are. Its
      `check-unresolved-threads` is a STUB that always returns
      {:has-unresolved? false}, making the :require-no-unresolved-threads?
      policy key inert; either implement it or delete the key, but do
      not leave an inert policy knob in a governance product.

  DEPLOY — what changes:
    * `phase-deployment/deploy.clj` `enter-deploy` goes
      resolve-deploy-config -> capture-current-state ->
      `kustomize-apply!` with NO policy gate (verified). After this
      spec the apply requires an :effect/deploy grant and an allow
      envelope.
    * `phase_deployment/policy.clj` `check-resource-count` and
      `check-gke-node-limit` EXIST and are never called from
      `enter-deploy`. Wire them as constraint inputs rather than
      writing new checks.
    * Fix the rollback-evidence drop: `store-apply-failure` currently
      discards `:evidence/rollback-info`, losing the undo artifact
      precisely on failure. Attach it on BOTH branches.
    * `kustomize-apply!` already accepts dry-run? and `enter-deploy`
      never passes it. The proposal stage SHOULD render the dry-run
      diff into :effect/proposal so the record says what was about to
      change.

  OUT OF SCOPE, deliberately: git push, PR create, and the resume
  webhook. They are irreversible too, but the RFC names three, and
  widening the blast radius of a single migration spec is how
  migrations stall. The webhook already documents at-least-once
  delivery with an acknowledged duplicate risk; push and PR-create get
  their own follow-up once this pattern has proven itself on merge.

  ALSO FOUND, NOT FIXED HERE (filed as follow-ups):
  `compliance_scanner/execute.clj` `execute-rule-fix!` ignores the exit
  code of both `git push` and `gh pr create` and returns
  (str/trim (:out pr-result)) as :pr-url — an empty string on failure,
  reported as success. That is a correctness bug independent of
  Ariadne and should not be smuggled into this spec."

 :spec/intent {:type :feature
               :scope ["components/pr-lifecycle/src/ai/miniforge/pr_lifecycle/merge.clj"
                       "components/pr-lifecycle/src/ai/miniforge/pr_lifecycle/controller.clj"
                       "components/phase-deployment/src/ai/miniforge/phase_deployment/deploy.clj"
                       "components/phase-deployment/src/ai/miniforge/phase_deployment/policy.clj"]}

 :spec/constraints
 ["No effect fires without an active grant and an allow (or allow-with-obligations) envelope"
  "No success is reported that the code cannot substantiate - enabling auto-merge is not merging"
  "Published SHAs come from reconciliation against GitHub, never from local git rev-parse"
  "Reuse phase_deployment/policy.clj's existing checks as constraint inputs; do not write parallel ones"
  "Rollback evidence is attached on the failure branch as well as the success branch"
  "Spend is NOT given a per-call proposal record - it is bounded by the 2b cost constraint"
  "Stratified design, max 3 layers per file"]

 :spec/acceptance-criteria
 ["merge-pr! with no active :effect/merge grant denies and fires no gh command"
  "A merge with a valid grant writes a durable proposal record before any gh invocation"
  "Enabling auto-merge yields :effect/state :committing - a test asserts it does NOT yield a merged claim"
  "The merged event is published only after reconcile! observes the merge on GitHub"
  "The published merge SHA equals the reconciled mergeCommit, and a test proves it differs from local HEAD in a squash scenario"
  "kustomize-apply! with no active :effect/deploy grant denies and runs no kubectl command"
  "check-resource-count and check-gke-node-limit are consulted before the apply"
  ":evidence/rollback-info is present on the ctx after a FAILED apply, not just a successful one"
  "The deploy proposal record carries the dry-run rendered diff"
  "full bb test green"]

 :spec/priority
 {:tier :high
  :axes #{:correctness :observation :governance-credibility}
  :theme :ariadne-grants
  :rationale "This is where step 2 becomes real behavior rather than available machinery; high rather than blocker because 2e can proceed in parallel once the coordinator lands."
  :blocks []
  :blocked-by ["ariadne-effect-transaction.spec.edn"]}

 :spec/workflow-type :canonical-sdlc}
